---
// Who connects to whom in an installation on AWS. The arrows point the way a connection is
// opened: nothing opens one into a runner or into a workspace.
---
<figure class="diagram">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 760 400" role="img" aria-labelledby="arch-t arch-d">
		<title id="arch-t">An installation on AWS</title>
		<desc id="arch-d">Users reach the proxy on 443. The proxy forwards to the control plane on 8080. Runners dial out to the control plane and to the proxy's relay; nothing dials into a runner. The control plane runs PostgreSQL on its own machine and archives it to an S3 bucket of its own; volumes live in another S3 bucket. Both are reached through the VPC's gateway endpoint.</desc>
		<defs>
			<marker id="arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
				<path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="var(--sl-color-gray-3)" />
			</marker>
		</defs>
		<rect class="box" x="20" y="40" width="120" height="56" rx="8" />
		<text class="t" x="80" y="64" text-anchor="middle">You, an agent</text>
		<text class="s" x="80" y="82" text-anchor="middle">dashboard, CLI, API</text>

		<rect class="zone" x="180" y="16" width="560" height="368" rx="12" />
		<text class="z" x="196" y="36">Your AWS account · one VPC</text>

		<rect class="accent" x="200" y="46" width="150" height="56" rx="8" />
		<text class="t" x="275" y="70" text-anchor="middle">Proxy</text>
		<text class="s" x="275" y="88" text-anchor="middle">Caddy, TLS, relay</text>

		<rect class="accent" x="420" y="46" width="160" height="56" rx="8" />
		<text class="t" x="500" y="70" text-anchor="middle">Control plane</text>
		<text class="s" x="500" y="88" text-anchor="middle">API, scheduler, PostgreSQL</text>

		<rect class="box" x="620" y="46" width="100" height="56" rx="8" />
		<text class="t" x="670" y="70" text-anchor="middle">S3</text>
		<text class="s" x="670" y="88" text-anchor="middle">database archive</text>

		<rect class="zone" x="200" y="170" width="380" height="190" rx="10" />
		<text class="z" x="214" y="190">Runners · autoscaling group, 0..n</text>
		<rect class="box" x="216" y="202" width="168" height="140" rx="8" />
		<text class="t" x="300" y="224" text-anchor="middle">Runner</text>
		<rect class="accent" x="230" y="236" width="140" height="28" rx="6" />
		<text class="s" x="300" y="254" text-anchor="middle">workspace · KVM VM</text>
		<rect class="accent" x="230" y="270" width="140" height="28" rx="6" />
		<text class="s" x="300" y="288" text-anchor="middle">workspace · KVM VM</text>
		<text class="s" x="300" y="326" text-anchor="middle">local NVMe cache</text>
		<rect class="box" x="400" y="202" width="164" height="140" rx="8" />
		<text class="t" x="482" y="224" text-anchor="middle">Runner</text>
		<rect class="accent" x="414" y="236" width="136" height="28" rx="6" />
		<text class="s" x="482" y="254" text-anchor="middle">workspace · KVM VM</text>

		<rect class="box" x="604" y="250" width="126" height="56" rx="8" />
		<text class="t" x="667" y="274" text-anchor="middle">S3</text>
		<text class="s" x="667" y="292" text-anchor="middle">volumes, Object Lock</text>

		<path class="line" d="M140 70H198" marker-end="url(#arr)" />
		<text class="s" x="148" y="62">443</text>
		<path class="line" d="M350 74H418" marker-end="url(#arr)" />
		<text class="s" x="364" y="66">8080</text>
		<path class="line" d="M580 74H618" marker-end="url(#arr)" />
		<path class="line" d="M300 200V104" marker-end="url(#arr)" />
		<text class="s" x="306" y="140">relay</text>
		<path class="line" d="M482 200V104" marker-end="url(#arr)" />
		<text class="s" x="488" y="140">dials out</text>
		<path class="line" d="M566 278H602" marker-end="url(#arr)" />
		<path class="line" d="M580 94Q640 150 660 248" marker-end="url(#arr)" />
	</svg>
	<figcaption>Arrows point the way a connection is opened. The proxy is the only machine the internet reaches; nothing opens a connection into a runner or a workspace.</figcaption>
</figure>
